  <model metaid="meta_rivaroxaban_coagulation" id="rivaroxaban_coagulation" name="Model for coagulation factors and readouts." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for coagulation factors and readouts.</p>
        <p>The effects depend on the total concentration of rivaroxaban in the venous
plasma <code>Cve_riv</code>, as the assays measure the total drug in a plasma sample.
The prothrombin time (PT) is linear in the concentration (Neoplastin, up
to the concentrations of 80 mg, Kubitza2005a, Mueck2014); the activated
partial thromboplastin time (aPTT) and the inhibition of factor Xa follow
an Emax model of the concentration, the PT and the aPTT relative to their
baseline (<code>PT_ref</code>, <code>aPTT_ref</code>), which an experiment sets to the baseline
of its subjects.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
